'''Andarum''' is a [[Ramu language]] of [[Papua New Guinea]]. Together with closely related [[Kanggape language|Kanggape]], there were about 4,000 speakers in 2000.<ref name=e25/>

According to an earlier classification, it belonged to the Ataitan languages (now renamed tanggu) and to the broader goam group, which also included 7 Tamolan languages, of which itutang (mzu) lost its status and was annexed to inapang [mzu] as its dialect.

It is related to the Kanggape language [igm]. Members of the ethnic group are called Andarum.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/2011/http://www.ethnologue.com/show_language.asp?code=aod Ethnologue (16th)]</ref>

